  "title": "Present active indicative: λύω",
  "note": "The verb ending shows the person, so a pronoun is rarely needed: λύω I loose, λύεις you loose, λύει he, she or it looses, λύομεν we loose, λύετε you (plural) loose, λύουσι(ν) they loose. Dictionaries list a verb by its first person singular. 'Not' is οὐ, which becomes οὐκ before a smooth breathing and οὐχ before a rough one.",
